[38;5;231m⏺[39m This is a bounded change: one existing page, rendered from inline data, and the filter can run in the browser. So I'll
  put a short design here in chat instead of writing a spec, and I won't start building until you say yes to it.

  Before the design, I need to know where the controls go. I've sketched three placements in a browser tab, which should
  have opened on its own. If it didn't, use this link:

  [94m]8;id=npjnls;http://localhost:53847/?key=39d96bcaf90f770a1fae34eee02acf14a813994ea135db4307d30c2954aae420\http://localhost:53847/?key=39d96bcaf90f770a1fae34eee02acf14a813994ea135db4307d30c2954aae420[39m]8;;\

  - [1mA. Filter bar above the table.[0m Event type, date range, and search are always visible in one row, which wraps on
    narrow screens. A result count sits underneath.
  - [1mB. A "Filter" button that opens a panel.[0m The page stays compact. Active filters show as removable tags next to the
    button, but you need a click to see the controls.
  - [1mC. Quick-filter tags plus a search field.[0m One-click views such as "Failed sign-ins" or "Account changes". This is
    the fastest way to find a failed sign-in, which is what the support tickets were about, but it's less precise.

  I'd go with A. Filters hidden behind a button work against "nobody can find anything", and A can still include a
  one-click "Failed sign-ins" option. Tell me here which one you want, or what you'd change. You can also click an
  option in the browser.

  Two side notes:
  - The sketches were saved under [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m in the project root. The repo has no [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m, so add [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m to
    one to keep those files out of commits.
  - The browser sketches use a lot of tokens. Say so if you'd rather do the rest in the terminal.

